# Reply and thread fixtures (PR 3.4), hand-written from Twitch's documented tags. One conversation in
# #testchan: a root message (R1), three replies in its thread (the second answers the first
# reply, so its reply-parent-* tags name that reply while reply-thread-parent-* still name R1),
# a reply whose parent is not in this log, and a reply with a very long parent body.
# reply-parent-msg-body is IRC-escaped on the wire (\s = space). Messages are 1.2 s apart.
# Tests: crates/twitch/src/parse/tests.rs (they refer to messages by id).
@emote-only=0;followers-only=-1;r9k=0;room-id=1000;slow=0;subs-only=0 :tmi.twitch.tv ROOMSTATE #testchan
